# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leaderboard configuration
#
# The global board is ON by default and needs no configuration — it points at
# our own Cloudflare Pages Function (`functions/api/scores.ts`), which ships
# with the site. There is no API key, no third-party SDK and no secret here.
#
# Override this only if you are running the board somewhere else (a preview
# deployment, a fork, or `wrangler pages dev` on localhost):
#
#   VITE_LB_API=http://localhost:8788/api/scores
#
# Set it to an empty string to force the purely local, offline board.
#
# ONE SHARED BOARD: both control setups (TWO HANDS / ONE HAND) write to the same
# table. A device owns exactly one row, keyed by a random UUID in localStorage,
# and the server's upsert keeps MAX(score) so a worse run can never lower it.
#
# The board degrades gracefully: if the network is unavailable the client falls
# back to the localStorage board and the leaderboard screen says so.
#
# NOTE: builds up to 1.0 used PlayFab (title 1095E4). Its free tier is capped
# at 1,000 lifetime player accounts and the app creates one per device, so the
# board moved here.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
VITE_LB_API=
